{
  "id": "st-ines",
  "name": "St. Ines",
  "module": "dark-coast",
  "summary": "A four-marine squad lands on the beach, crosses the canal into the old city, reaches St. Ines Hospital, and brings the survivors out to the dropship.",
  "briefing": [
    "Port Ines stopped transmitting thirty hours ago. A distress beacon is still pinging from St. Ines Hospital, six blocks inland from Red Beach.",
    "Your squad goes in alone: one dropship, Halyard, will hold just offshore of Red Beach and can take everyone you bring back. It can't come inland.",
    "Get across the canal, get into the hospital, find whoever set off that beacon, and get them to the beach. Nobody knows what's in the streets. Assume the worst and move like it.",
    "Squad leader, you have the radio. Everyone else: if you lose sight of your sergeant, you're on your own until you find them again."
  ],
  "refereeNotes": "Nine survivors are barricaded on the hospital's second floor with a wounded nurse; a crawler is in the basement and will take anyone who goes looking for the generator. Three more people are holed up in the pharmacy, with shamblers pressing at the shutters. One group of shamblers is in the open across the canal at the start and can be seen from the beach. Runners are lying up in the old town to the northeast; they come at noise. Raise the threat when the squad is loud, or slow. The bridge is the only way over the canal for anyone carrying a stretcher.",
